            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The \"customize tabstop placeholders\" is a bit vague, but I am pretty sure that it is already possible with 'mini.snippets':\n- If you mean customize `•` and `∎` characters that are shown as virtual text for empty tabstops, then this is possible via [`empty_tabstop` and `empty_tabstop_final` options of `default_insert`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d570e0b01aabfe949c097983ed6386af60db32ed/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1109-L1112). Here is an [example of how to do this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d570e0b01aabfe949c097983ed6386af60db32ed/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L698-L701).\n- If you mean highlighting of tabstops (colored underdouble by default), then those are adjusted via [highlight groups](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d570e0b01aabfe949c097983ed6386af60db32ed/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L120-L124).\n- If you mean adjust text of a placeholder that is used in snippet, then this is done by adjusting snippet data itself.\n\nAll in all, I am pretty sure that this is already possible in 'mini.snippets', so closing it. If you meant something different from what is listed above, please, leave a comment.",
            "created_at": "2025-04-06T11:55:26Z",
